  "translation": "This afternoon, my friend and I went to a supermarket we often go to together. We set out from home and first went to the fruit section. My friend asked the shop assistant, 'We don't know what fruit to buy, apples or oranges? Where are the apples? How much is one?' The shop assistant pointed to the shelf on the front left and said, 'The apples are right there, with a label on top. One costs two yuan.' My friend said, 'Great, we'll buy three apples, and also buy a bottle of water.' I said, 'OK, the water is on the shelf on the right, I'll go get one too.' I took a bottle of water and put it in the shopping cart. While we were selecting, the shop assistant said, 'There's a promotion now: if you can buy three bottles of water, you get a pack of tissues for free.' My friend asked, 'Really? Then we'll buy two more bottles.' So we took two more bottles of water. When we went to pay, the cashier said, 'The total is fifteen yuan.' I gave her a hundred yuan, and she gave me eighty-five yuan change. We all went home very happily."
